<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad, Count Palatine of the Rhine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1135–1195</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Conrad of Hohenstaufen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> was count palatine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> from 1156 until his death in 1195, a half-brother of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>. He built up a territorial base around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alzey">Alzey</a> and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a>, laying the foundation of the later Electoral Palatinate. Through his daughter Agnes, who married Henry of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, the palatinate passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a>.</p></div>
